(a) Commission's mandate to conduct a survey of local historical resources. The commission shall compile and collect information and conduct surveys of historic resources within the city.
(b) Commission's power to recommend districts and landmarks to the mayor and board of aldermen for designation. The commission shall present to the mayor and board of aldermen its nominations for historic districts and historic landmarks.
(c) Preparation of report on proposed designations. Prior to the commission's recommendation of a historic landmark or historic district to the mayor and board of aldermen for designation, the commission shall prepare formal reports, which shall also be used to educate the community and to provide a permanent record of the proposed designation, and shall consist of:
(1) A physical description;
(2) A statement of the historical, cultural, architectural and/or aesthetic significance;
(3) A map showing district boundaries and classification (i.e., historic, nonhistoric, intrusion) of individual properties, or showing boundaries of individual historic properties;
(4) A statement justifying district or individual property boundaries; and
(5) Representative photographs, if necessary for clarification.
This report will be submitted to the historic preservation section of the state department of natural resources and the mayor and board of aldermen.
(Code 1983, § 15-35(a))

